thought on these matters.
BUT, morality motivates people in a way that logic and practicality
does not. So, it might be worth using moralitic language, in order to 
persuade. 

(Controversy warning!)
Perhaps the distinction between the moral and practical aspects is overdrawn.
Oddly, perhaps uniquely, some post-modernist philosophers agree with Ayn
Rand on this one - they both see a connection. (Dare I hope for no flames? 8-O 
