This does not mean that I think that believing Quantum Physics implies a clear 
moral code. As usual, the meme-sphere concept helps me express it best. The 
universe (reality) and the world of ideas (meme-sphere) are loosely coupled 
adaptive systems. Each perturbs the other, without containing or determining it.

That said, I'm still much more comfortable talking about the practical/logical 
aspects. (INTP!) Rights coevolve with memes and institutions.




