Date:        Sun, 28 Mar 93 13:05:57 EST
From: I151000 <I151%NEMOMUS.BITNET@mitvma.mit.edu>
Subject: BRAIN: Sound & Light Machines

   I have not had any experience with sound and light machines, but have
experimented with similiar machines.  I believe that most of the
machines out there use photic and sonic driving to induce various
brain-wave patterns.  Back in high school I read about the technology
that is used in the sonic-driving tapes and machines.  Basically,
different tones are presented to each ear and the brain combines them
(this in itself is extremely interesting), and begins to exibit a
greater percentage of brain waves equal to the difference between the
two tones.  For instance, if I were to present your left ear with a 400
Hz tone, and your right ear with a 404 Hz tone, your brain would begin
to exibit more 4 Hz (low Delta, if I remember correctly) than normal.  I
don't know too much about photic driving, but I'd guess that the
frequency of the flashing lighs would roughly correspond to the brain
waves emitted.
   Robert Monroe has extensivly pioneered this area, especially in
relation to altered states of conciousness.  He is a bit on the flaky
side, as the research is geared towards inducing out-of-body
experiences, but his research has produced some interesting results.
See "Far Journeys" for more info.
   It's very simple to program your computer (particularily if you've
got an Amiga) to produce different tones for each ear.  A simple Basic
program was all it took for my Amiga.  I used the sonic-driving theory
to produce "Shumann Resonance", (7.83 Hz) and taped it.  I found that
when listening to the tape with headphones, it was much easier to
concentrate upon any intellectual tasks at hand (this could have been
simply because the sound drowned out any distractions, but it SEEMED as
if my concentration was enhanced).  Informal self-expirementation showed
that I did significantly better on tests that I had studied for while
using the tape, particularily those requiring rote memorization.
   Meditation using the same tape was much more effective.  Autogenic
shift can be accomplish extremely quickly after using sonic-driving for
about a month.  After awhile, it becomes possible to aquire the
autogenic shift without the use of the tape.
   Instead of paying through the nose for a mind/brain machine, you may
be better off in making you own tapes or ordering some from Monroe's
outfit.  I have the address around here somewhere - tell me if you'd
like it.



