Subject: VR: question re: P. Science

	With regards to sound/light brain machines, I think that I should 
mention an amazing toy that my girlfriend bought recently. It is simply a 
mask (divers mask style), with two holes for eyes, and a rotating disc, also
with two similar holes. There is a small mouth straw, which you blow in to
make the disc rotate. You look at the sun with your eyes closed, and blow into
the straw to make the disc rotate, so you get several short flashes per second,
as holes in the disc line up with the holes in the mask. This makes absolutely
astonishing color patterns, with quite an array of colors. I don't know about
any other effects, but it sure is fun. It appears to be made here in Western
Australia, and at $AUS20 (about $US15, I think) it is much better value than
any of the powered mind amchines if you just want to fool around.
